ted): R / [(π/N)^3 S_HL_full(0,h_1,h_2)] within 1% across all 6 admissible (h_1, h_2) tested at d=20. F4 self-consistency at h_1 = h_2 = 0: ratio = 1.00000 ± 1e-5. F5 (h_2 = 0 reduces to S205 pair × W/φ(W)): exact algebraic identity. F6 (prime triple density): 5% deviation from full HL at d=20 (standard finite-N rate). **What's new beyond S205**: S205 covers the 2-point shift case via diagonal q1=q2 contraction; S210 extends to 3-point shift where the diagonal contraction is INSUFFICIENT (off-diagonal cross-pair terms contribute essentially), but the divisor-restricted T_W^{div} factorises cleanly via S208's Möbius collapse, giving exact closed form at primorial W. **What's new beyond S208**: S208 was the 1-point identity (M_W^{div}(n) = [gcd=1]·W/φ(W)); S210 promotes this to the 3-point correlation, exhibiting the wheel-W indicator's 3-point function as exactly the prime-3-tuple HL singular series at conductor W. **What's new beyond E2.13**: E2.13 is the 4-point cube U^2 / HL match; S210 is the 3-point shift identity, a different observable in the Schwinger-Dyson hierarchy not derivable from E2.13. **What's new beyond E2.16**: E2.16 ruled out kernel-DPP/PPP descriptions of primes by noting 3-point HL factors over primes (not pairs); S210 exhibits the explicit pointwise scalar field T_W^{div} whose 3-point function REALISES this prime-factored 3-tuple singular series — turning E2.16's negative shape into a positive identity. **No polylog opening**: cost is O(N · |H|^2) per (h_1, h_2) batch on T_W^{div}; the construction provides a closed-form numerical evaluator of S_HL^{(W)} at O(W · |H|²) cost (faster than any direct prime-triple sieve), but is structural not algorithmic. **Cross-domain ingredient**: NONE — paradigm-shift session mode forbade cross-domain imports. The argument uses only Möbius inclusion-exclusion (S208), Ramanujan sums (S205), and direct prime-by-prime factorisation. **Falsifier**: any primorial W and admissible (h_1, h_2) with R_emp / pred outside [0.99, 1.01] at d ≥ 18 — empirically falsified to <0.01% across 5×12×3 = 180 cells. OR exhibition of polylog evaluation of ⟨T_W^{div}(n) T_W^{div}(n+h_1) T_W^{div}(n+h_2)⟩ at W ≈ √N as primality-triple witness — would resolve polylog π(x). **Successors (S210)**: C9.b.iv (k=4 four-point at primorial W, predicted closed form (π/N)^4 · ∏_{p|W} (p − ν_p) p^3 / (p−1)^4, 1 session); C9.b.v (general-Q off-diagonal calibration: predict the F2 over-count from missing subsets analytically, 1 session); C9.b.vi (Lean formalisation of the 3-point identity via the S208 Möbius collapse + 3-coprimality factorisation, ~30-line Lean target, 1-2 sessions). See `experiments/constructions/spike_pointwise_HL_triple/`, `archive/sessions/session210_c9b_ii_triple_correlation.md`. | 210 |
