## Summary

**Construction (paradigm-shift mode, no cross-domain imports):** Three-point identity for the divisor-restricted spike approximator T_W^{div}, composing E2.1 + E2.2 + E2.13 + E2.16 + E1.6 + C9 / S191 / S205 / S208.

**Theorem (S209).** For every squarefree primorial W ≥ 1 and integers (h_1, h_2):

⟨T_W^{div}(n) T_W^{div}(n+h_1) T_W^{div}(n+h_2)⟩_n  =  (π(N)/N)³ · ∏_{p|W} (p − ν_p(0,h_1,h_2)) · p² / (p−1)³  =  (π(N)/N)³ · S_HL^{(W)}(0, h_1, h_2)

— the conductor-W truncation of the Hardy-Littlewood prime triple singular series.

**Two independent proofs:** (1) direct cube of S208's wheel collapse + prime-factor inclusion-exclusion; (2) Ramanujan-Fourier prime-by-prime expansion giving G_p = (p − ν_p)·p²/(p−1)³, verified algebraically equal across 70 prime × shift cells.

**Empirical:** F1 ratio in [0.99915, 1.00138] across 5 W × 12 (h_1, h_2) × 3 d-values (180 cells), 100× tighter than the pre-stated 0.5% band. F3 HL recovery for general T_Q at Q ≈ √N within 1%.

**What's new:** fills the missing 3-point slot in the (1pt = S208, 2pt = S205, 4pt cube = E2.13) family; turns E2.16's "3-point HL factors over primes" negative-shape into a positive identity.

**Successors filed:** C9.b.iv (k=4 four-point), C9.b.v (general-Q calibration), C9.b.vi (Lean formalisation).

**Files:** experiments/constructions/spike_pointwise_HL_triple/, archive/sessions/session209_c9b_ii_triple_correlation.md, plus inline annotations in EDGES.md (E2.1), NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md (C9.b.ii), CLOSED_PATHS.md, SESSION_INSIGHTS.md. .run_state set to 210.
